PART 1c  Legendre-coefficient route and the DME 13-energy nodes
==============================================================================
4 lowest-order complex Legendre coefficients already reproduce the dense complex amplitude to max 9.5618e-05 (grid RMS 1.2934e-05);
coefs of order >=4 are < 1.12e-05, i.e. at/just above the 1e-5 storage quantum. The dense grid is a 4-parameter (per energy) angular object.
control, same 13-node construction applied directly to the stored magnitude: natural 0.1932, linear 0.2685

Linear map DME(7 complex) -> 4 complex Legendre coefs across the 13 measured energies: 15 real parameters for 104 real targets, rank 13, max residual 3.109e-15 -> the 4 coefficients at the measured energies are an exact linear function of the DME block.
   => the 13 'measured' rows are consistent with a direct algebraic construction from the DME blocks, not with the raw arrays.

